=============================
📌 EP03 – FOR-IN LOOPS IN DART
=============================

🔷 1️⃣ What is a For-In Loop?

A for-in loop is used to read all elements in a list/set one by one, without using an index.

👉 Best when you want to only read values
👉 No need to write i < list.length
👉 No need to write i++

🔷 2️⃣ Basic Syntax

for (var item in collection) {
  // use item
}

✔ item → each value
✔ collection → list/set/map keys

🔷 3️⃣ Example 1: Simple List Loop

List<String> names = ["Ram", "Shyam", "Mohan"];

for (var name in names) {          // For-In reads each value
  print(name);                     // Print each name
}

📌 Output:
Ram
Shyam
Mohan

💡 Why use?

Cleaner and shorter than normal for loop when you don’t need index.

🔷 4️⃣ Example 2: Numbers List

List<int> numbers = [10, 20, 30];

for (var n in numbers) {
  print("Value is: $n");          // Use each number
}

📌 Output:
Value is: 10
Value is: 20
Value is: 30

🔷 5️⃣ Real-Life Example 1: Show all items in a shopping cart

List<String> cart = ["Shoes", "Watch", "Cap"];

for (var item in cart) {
  print("Cart item: $item");
}

🔷 6️⃣ Real-Life Example 2: Send email to all users

List<String> emails = ["a@gmail.com", "b@gmail.com", "c@gmail.com"];

for (var email in emails) {
  print("Sending email to: $email");
}


🔷 7️⃣ For-In with Set (No duplicate values)

Set<String> fruits = {"Apple", "Mango", "Banana"};

for (var fruit in fruits) {
  print(fruit);
}


🔷 8️⃣ For-In with Map Keys

Map<String, int> scores = {
  "Math": 90,
  "Science": 85,
  "English": 88
};

for (var subject in scores.keys) {
  print("Subject: $subject");
}


🔷 9️⃣ For-In with Map Values

for (var score in scores.values) {
  print("Score: $score");
}

🔷 🔟 For-In with Map (Key + Value)

for (var entry in scores.entries) {
  print("${entry.key}: ${entry.value}");
}


🟩 1️⃣1️⃣ When should we use For-In Loop?

✔ When you don’t need the index
✔ When reading list, set, or map
✔ When code should look cleaner
✔ When order is important (list)